# GDevelop Custom AI - Browser Development Environment Variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your API keys.
# These variables are used when running the browser dev server (npm start).
#
# IMPORTANT: 
# - Never commit `.env.local` to version control!
# - The `.env.local` file is already in .gitignore.
# - Create React App only exposes variables prefixed with REACT_APP_
# - You must restart the dev server after changing this file

# OpenAI API Key (for browser dev server)
# Get your key from: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# Format: sk-proj-... or sk-...
REACT_APP_GDEVELOP_OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Anthropic API Key (for browser dev server)
# Get your key from: https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
# Format: sk-ant-...
REACT_APP_GDEVELOP_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Usage:
# 1. Copy this file: cp .env.local.example .env.local
# 2. Edit .env.local and add your API keys
# 3. Restart the dev server: npm start
# 4. Hard refresh the browser (Cmd+Shift+R or Ctrl+Shift+R)
#
# Notes:
# - These REACT_APP_* variables are for the BROWSER dev server only
# - For the Electron app, use newIDE/electron-app/.env.local with GDEVELOP_* variables
# - Environment variables take precedence over keys stored in the app
# - Keys are never logged or sent to GDevelop servers
# - Whitespace is automatically trimmed from values
# - Empty values are treated as "not set"
#
# For more information, see: _docs/CUSTOM_AI_ENV_VARS.md

